// REJECTS: Execution param key cannot contain spaces. Invalid Key: UAT env
//
// An execution-environment key is an `identifier`, and `identifier` admits a quoted STRING,
// so 'UAT env' lexes and parses perfectly. The walker then refuses it because the key is
// used as a lookup name.
//
// Nothing in the .g4 expresses this. A generated parser accepts the quoted form
// unconditionally -- which is the whole category this corpus exists to catch.
###Service
ExecutionEnvironment fixture::neg::EnvKeyWithSpace
{
   executions:
   [
      'UAT env':
      {
         mapping: fixture::neg::M;
         runtime: fixture::neg::R;
      }
   ];
}
